<title>BELGIUM: Volanen set to be appointed COPA farm chief.</title>
<headline>Volanen set to be appointed COPA farm chief.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finn Risto Volanen is expected to be appointed on Friday secretary general of COPA, the EU farmers' organisation, COPA sources said.</p>
<p>They said that Volanen, aged 52, deputy director general of Finnish cooperative Tellervo, was the only candidate for the post which will decided at a meeting of COPA and COGECA, farm cooperative, national delegates.</p>
<p>The post was vacated by Frenchman Daniel Gueguen in early 1996. Englishman Peter Pooley stood in as acting secretary general for several months.</p>
</text>
